  "term": "paralysis agitans",
  "definition": "Paralysis agitans is an older name for Parkinson disease, a progressive degenerative neurologic disorder. It involves tremor that is strongest at rest, rigidity, slowed voluntary movement, stooped posture, a tendency to fall backward, and a reduced facial expression.",
